# Notes and Vault public proof verifier

This is a finite, read-only integrity verifier for the installed notebook-trash and entry recycle-bin followups. The public module is `scripts/verify-notes-vault-followups.mjs` in the lab repository. It exports `verifyNotesVaultFollowups(labRoot)` and has an optional `--standalone` entry point. It reads public snapshots only and does not execute an original program, application runtime, host, or browser. Private work folders, local original binaries and native fixture carriers are not prerequisites.

The pinned final Notes plan has 26 strict artifacts and maps 935 source paths to 920 published inert files plus 15 explicit local-only 9,728-byte JEX/TAR copies of one authenticated digest. Its preceding 25-artifact plan and erroneous prospective 73 total remain separately authenticated historical records; the final prospective total is 59. The four original Notes inventories contain 927 records, with eight manifest/freeze self-carriers. The verifier checks every original row against exactly one published or excluded mapping and checks the published epoch file inventories.

The pinned Vault plan has 45 strict artifacts and maps 858 source paths to 857 publishable path records, representing 471 unique public paths: 444 new inert objects and 27 exact existing-history reuses. One 1,911-byte synthetic KDBX remains explicitly local-only. The four original inventories contain 850 records and eight manifest/freeze self-carriers. Four retained `.png` path aliases contain JPEG bytes beginning `FF D8 FF`; the verifier authenticates and preserves that historical mapping rather than relabeling the files.

All 34 installed runtime, test, helper and documentation proposals are authenticated against the frozen root installation and the final public plans. Seven Notes adapters and seven Vault adapters are mechanically reconstructed from preserved inputs using the exact path/output-location substitutions. Exact source copies remain byte-identical; documentation proposals have their own exact preserved identities. The 11 installed preexisting before-images resolve to the immutable 455 checkpoint, independently of current source. The Vault plan's 31-file pre-install source baseline resolves 30 files to that checkpoint. Its `KDBX-COVERAGE.md` was not captured there and is separately authenticated against the pinned plan identity and unchanged current bytes.

The original 159 source SHA identities and 232 capability IDs are compared to both final plan projections. Entire current registry hashes are interval observations, not immutable old-plan assertions: parent metadata may evolve without changing those identities. No historical receipt is rebound to current code. The existing root `verify-followup-records.mjs`, all application files and public results remain unchanged by this task.

The final collection records 12 passing source-only integrity cases, zero failures or skips, and exact verifier/test/runner source before and after. A temporary anonymous-public mirror contains only files observed by verification. Cases reject corrupted original source, shared blobs, exclusion/map edits, installed adapters, immutable before-images, extra plan files, changed original registry identities, and mid-interval mutations. Metadata-only evolution is a positive control. Pure guards cover nine unsafe paths and four native carrier headers; JPEG remains an allowed inert image. These are verifier regressions, not additional app behavioral tests or original parity comparisons.

Six direct verifier-development failures are preserved with exact candidate snapshots: incorrect self-carrier filename assumption; null/undefined exclusion assumption; old-history manifest field assumption; the 30-versus-31 checkpoint denominator; visual-registry schema assumption; and the freeze record's receipt/validation representation. A first child run inherited `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` and executed no tests; the environment field is removed entirely in the correction. A second run passed all 12 tests but used Node's default spec reporter, so the TAP-only recorder could not certify its summary. Its raw output stays separate. The final run explicitly selects TAP and records 12/12. Source-discovery/path errors and a premature attempt to inspect a still-running receipt are tool diagnostics, not implementation failures.

Every read is capped at 32 MiB, unique read bytes at 512 MiB, and unique files at 10,000; proof inventories are bounded and disallow traversal, `.local` public segments, nonregular files and discovered reparse/symlink paths. The verifier rereads all identities after the finite interval. These checks do not establish a hard disk-I/O deadline or race-free filesystem sandbox. The owned regression collector has a 150-second child deadline and 1 MiB stdout/stderr caps; generic Windows descendant isolation is not claimed. No timing or memory comparison was performed.

The original source and license records remain in the exact published Notes and Vault mappings. This verifier does not redistribute native original programs or fixtures. Full product parity, security parity and universal superiority remain false. Actual Notes native confirmation browser acceptance is still incomplete in the retained review; the parent may add separately bound later acceptance evidence.
